1) Review primary legislation.
2) Verify the particular situation in the State regarding judicial investigations, and its impact on the ability of the State to comply with Annex 13.
3) Verify the existence of a competent authority able to administer a balancing test to determine whether the disclosure or use of accident and incident investigation records outweighs the likely adverse domestic and international impact such action may have on that or any future investigations.
4) Records in the custody or control of the accident investigation authority that are to be protected include:
a) cockpit voice recordings and airborne image recordings and any transcripts from such recordings;
b) records from interviews with persons by the investigation authorities in the course of the investigation;
c) communications between persons having been involved in the operation of the aircraft;
d) medical or private information regarding persons involved in the accident or incident;
e) recordings and transcripts of recordings from air traffic control units;
f) analysis of and opinions about information (including flight recorder information) made by the accident investigation authority and accredited representatives in relation to the accident or incident; and
g) the draft final report of an accident or incident investigation.

1) Review legislation (primary aviation legislation or regulations).
2) Verify the particular situation in the State regarding judicial investigations, and its impact on the capacity of the State to comply with Annex 13.
3) Confirm that the participation of accredited representatives from the following States is permitted:
a) State of Registry;
b) State of Operator;
c) State of Design;
d) State of Manufacture; and
e) any other State which, on request, provides information, facilities or experts.
4) The entitlement must include the following:
a) visit the scene of the accident;
b) examine the wreckage;
c) obtain witness information and suggest areas of questioning;
d) have full access to all relevant evidence as soon as possible;
e) receive copies of all pertinent documents;
f) participate in read-outs of recorded media;
